WEBVTT

00:14.171 --> 00:16.171
-("Before I Ever Met You" by BANKS plays)
-(vocalizing)

00:22.338 --> 00:27.463
(vocalizing)

00:29.171 --> 00:31.671
(vocalizing)

00:31.755 --> 00:33.755
(instruments join in)

00:44.421 --> 00:50.213
♪ Everyone knows I'm right
about one thing ♪

00:50.338 --> 00:54.130
♪ You and I don't work out ♪

00:54.213 --> 00:56.130
(vocalizing)

00:56.213 --> 00:58.630
♪ You bring out the mean in me ♪

00:58.713 --> 01:01.838
♪ I bring out your insecurities ♪

01:01.921 --> 01:06.088
♪ You know what I am talking about ♪

01:06.171 --> 01:08.338
♪ ♪

01:21.130 --> 01:24.630
(vocalizing)

01:37.963 --> 01:39.963
(music stops)

01:43.088 --> 01:44.630
What?

01:48.671 --> 01:51.463
Nothing.

02:02.796 --> 02:04.796
(birds chirping)

02:14.630 --> 02:16.630
-(music resumes)
-(vocalizing)

02:26.796 --> 02:30.630
(vocalizing continues)

02:30.713 --> 02:32.713
(song ends)

02:37.713 --> 02:41.088
Alexa, play "Old MacDonald."

02:41.171 --> 02:44.671
-(Alexa chimes, song plays)
-♪ Old MacDonald had a farm ♪

02:44.755 --> 02:47.671
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

02:47.755 --> 02:50.671
-♪ And on his farm he had some ducks ♪
-Trixie!

02:50.755 --> 02:52.463
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

02:52.546 --> 02:54.171
-(doorbell rings)
-♪ With a quack quack here ♪

02:54.255 --> 02:55.838
-♪ And a quack quack there ♪
-Trixie, I'm not kidding.

02:55.921 --> 02:58.296
♪ Here a quack, there a quack,
everywhere a quack quack ♪

02:58.380 --> 03:00.171
-♪ Old MacDonald had a farm ♪
-Hey. -Hey.

03:00.255 --> 03:01.338
MELINDA:
Turn it off.

03:01.421 --> 03:03.046
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

03:03.130 --> 03:06.005
♪ And on his farm he had some cows ♪

03:06.088 --> 03:08.421
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

03:08.505 --> 03:10.630
-I'm so, so sorry I'm late, Mr. Van Allen.
-♪ With a moo moo here... ♪

03:10.713 --> 03:13.463
It's okay. Melinda's…
It's okay, Melinda's still getting ready.

03:13.546 --> 03:16.463
♪ Old MacDonald had a farm ♪

03:16.546 --> 03:19.380
-♪ E-I-E-I-O. ♪
-Alexa, stop!

03:19.463 --> 03:21.005
-(Alexa chimes, music stops)
-(laughs quietly)

03:21.088 --> 03:23.921
Don't play that shit ever again, please.

03:25.088 --> 03:26.338
Vic, can you come here?

03:26.421 --> 03:27.588
What?

03:27.671 --> 03:29.171
I need your help.

03:29.255 --> 03:32.380
Alexa, play "Old MacDonald" again.

03:32.463 --> 03:34.713
-(Alexa chimes, song plays)
-♪ Old MacDonald had a farm ♪

03:34.796 --> 03:37.338
Trixie, you're going to drive
your mom crazy, you know that?

03:37.421 --> 03:39.671
I know.

03:39.755 --> 03:41.588
-(chuckles)
-♪ And on his farm he had some ducks ♪

03:41.671 --> 03:43.963
-♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪
-VIC: Have a seat.

03:44.046 --> 03:45.338
-♪ With a quack quack here ♪
-Hey, Trixie.

03:45.421 --> 03:48.130
♪ And a quack quack there,
here a quack… ♪

03:48.213 --> 03:50.130
(song continues low in background)

03:50.213 --> 03:52.755
(Vic sighs)

03:53.838 --> 03:55.963
Don't look at the mess. Look at me.

03:56.046 --> 03:57.630
Yes.

03:57.713 --> 03:59.380
I don't know, I just...

03:59.463 --> 04:03.213
Should I wear this or this?

04:03.296 --> 04:05.296
Um…

04:06.296 --> 04:08.338
No? You don't like either?

04:08.421 --> 04:10.046
No, I'm just thinking.

04:12.171 --> 04:13.421
Hmm?

04:14.505 --> 04:16.630
I think you look beautiful
in the dress you have on.

04:17.796 --> 04:19.421
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

04:21.630 --> 04:23.171
Okay.

04:24.255 --> 04:26.671
(Melinda sighs)

04:26.755 --> 04:28.671
With what shoe?

04:28.755 --> 04:30.880
The black shoes I got you in New York.

04:33.338 --> 04:35.171
Okay.

04:36.921 --> 04:38.796
Go get them.

04:40.921 --> 04:42.296
Please.

04:42.380 --> 04:43.630
(softly):
Sure.

04:59.505 --> 05:02.130
Do you know I love you?

05:08.838 --> 05:10.796
Come on.

05:10.880 --> 05:12.630
Let's go.

05:12.713 --> 05:15.338
("Sneakin' Sally Through the Alley"
by Robert Palmer playing)

05:19.338 --> 05:22.838
-♪ Sneakin' Sally through the alley ♪
-(loud crowd chatter)

05:25.296 --> 05:28.130
-♪ Trying to keep her out of sight ♪
-MAN: Enjoy.

05:29.171 --> 05:31.213
♪ Sneakin' Sally through the alley... ♪

05:31.296 --> 05:34.213
We asked her
and she chose public school.

05:34.296 --> 05:36.171
-You let her choose?
-VIC: Mm-hmm.

05:36.255 --> 05:38.171
-She's six.
-I was kicked out

05:38.255 --> 05:41.421
of so many schools growing up,
I'm just grateful she wants an education.

05:42.421 --> 05:45.213
-You aren't worried about competition
for college? -VIC: College?

05:45.296 --> 05:48.255
The kid's brilliant. The worst thing
we could do is send her to college.

05:48.338 --> 05:50.380
(Melinda laughs)

05:50.463 --> 05:52.880
-♪ ♪
-(crowd chatter)

06:02.713 --> 06:04.046
Joel.

06:07.546 --> 06:10.463
BARTENDER:
So, uh, how you doing tonight?

06:11.421 --> 06:12.880
Hmm?

06:12.963 --> 06:15.671
No, I was just asking
how you're doing tonight.

06:16.755 --> 06:18.630
I'll let you know
after a few more of these.

06:21.921 --> 06:26.171
♪ Oh, when up pops the queen ♪

06:26.255 --> 06:28.838
♪ Trying to double talk,
get myself in trouble talk ♪

06:28.921 --> 06:31.130
♪ Catching myself in lies ♪

06:32.838 --> 06:36.005
♪ Catch myself in lies ♪

06:36.088 --> 06:40.921
♪ Mama just looked at me
as if I was, ah, crazy... ♪

06:41.005 --> 06:43.005
(band playing "Walking Blues")

06:49.421 --> 06:53.880
♪ I woke up this mornin',
lookin' round for my shoes, yeah ♪

06:53.963 --> 06:56.963
♪ You know that I have
them old walkin' blues... ♪

06:57.046 --> 06:58.755
JOEL:
Whoo.

06:58.838 --> 07:00.838
(low music playing)

07:10.880 --> 07:15.088
♪ He got Elgin movement
from his head down to his toes ♪

07:15.171 --> 07:19.255
♪ I bet he can make himself a dollar
anywhere he goes ♪

07:19.338 --> 07:21.088
♪ He got the Elgin movement... ♪

07:21.171 --> 07:23.171
(low music plays)

07:35.005 --> 07:37.005
♪ ♪

07:47.588 --> 07:49.588
(rock riff plays)

07:58.880 --> 08:00.880
(low chatter)

08:02.005 --> 08:03.630
Yo.

08:03.713 --> 08:07.088
Yo. How's it going?

08:07.171 --> 08:09.588
I'm getting a lot
of cleavage action tonight.

08:09.671 --> 08:11.838
-Hmm. I see that.
-(laughing)

08:13.671 --> 08:15.505
MARY:
Is that Joel with Melinda?

08:16.588 --> 08:18.213
VIC:
Yeah.

08:19.255 --> 08:22.130
They've really hit it off
in a short amount of time, haven't they?

08:22.213 --> 08:24.671
I guess they have.

08:27.380 --> 08:29.838
(laughs)
Hello, Mr. Boring.

08:29.921 --> 08:31.671
Why don't you dance?

08:31.755 --> 08:33.921
I'd hate to ruin your evening.

08:41.213 --> 08:45.171
You know he's only here because she asked
Jess and Grant to invite him here.

08:45.255 --> 08:46.963
She can invite whoever she wants.

08:47.046 --> 08:48.963
Vic...

08:49.046 --> 08:50.546
they fucking?

08:50.630 --> 08:52.338
-Should we ask them?
-Vic.

08:55.255 --> 08:57.171
They're friends.

08:57.255 --> 08:58.671
Aren't they just.

08:58.755 --> 09:00.671
(clicks tongue, inhales deeply)

09:00.755 --> 09:03.088
-I'm gonna just blurt it out, okay?
-Okay.

09:03.171 --> 09:04.546
A few of us are concerned.

09:04.630 --> 09:07.463
-You're concerned?
-Yes.

09:07.546 --> 09:08.880
That they're fucking?

09:08.963 --> 09:10.213
(laughs quietly)

09:10.296 --> 09:12.630
What if your concerns aren't my concerns?

09:14.713 --> 09:17.338
Look, you adore her and everyone knows it.

09:19.005 --> 09:21.255
-I love her.
-She loves you, too.

09:22.338 --> 09:24.505
You're good, Vic.

09:25.296 --> 09:28.046
We just don't want you out here
looking foolish.

09:29.713 --> 09:31.671
-I'll stay off the dance floor.
-(laughs)

09:31.755 --> 09:33.088
GRANT:
Vic. Hey.

09:33.171 --> 09:35.130
I'm sorry to interrupt, Mary, my bad,

09:35.213 --> 09:37.671
but, uh, Melinda's drunk

09:37.755 --> 09:39.338
and she's standing on top of my piano.

09:40.421 --> 09:42.213
-That concerns me.
-Yeah.

09:42.296 --> 09:43.921
-Whoo.
-(people cheering)

09:44.005 --> 09:45.255
MELINDA:
I like dancing though.

09:45.338 --> 09:48.588
-You could dance if you want.
-(excited chatter)

09:48.671 --> 09:50.671
Ya, ya, ya. Okay, okay.

09:50.755 --> 09:52.046
I-I don't know how to give toasts,

09:52.130 --> 09:54.880
so I'm going to climb down from this piano

09:54.963 --> 09:57.463
and how about if I play a song.

09:57.546 --> 09:59.421
-(whoops, cheers)
-Yeah?

10:01.755 --> 10:03.921
My husband's good at giving toasts.

10:04.005 --> 10:06.005
-PARTYGOER: Yeah, Vic!
-(shouts, cheers)

10:07.588 --> 10:10.630
(plays gentle melody)

10:13.130 --> 10:15.380
MELINDA (laughing):
Okay.

10:15.463 --> 10:17.046
Oh.

10:18.546 --> 10:21.088
(singing "Via Con Me" in Italian)

10:46.796 --> 10:50.296
(others joining in):
♪ It's wonderful, it's wonderful ♪

10:50.380 --> 10:52.296
♪ It's wonderful ♪

10:52.380 --> 10:54.630
♪ Good luck, my baby ♪

10:54.713 --> 10:57.963
♪ It's wonderful, it's wonderful ♪

10:58.046 --> 11:00.213
♪ It's wonderful ♪

11:00.296 --> 11:01.921
♪ I dream of you ♪

11:02.005 --> 11:05.046
♪ Chips, chips ♪

11:05.130 --> 11:08.338
♪ Doo, doo, doo-doo-doo,
ci-boom, ci-boom, boom ♪

11:08.421 --> 11:09.630
♪ Doo, doo, doo-doo-doo ♪

11:09.713 --> 11:12.046
♪ Ci-boom, ci-boom, boom ♪

11:12.130 --> 11:14.171
♪ Doo, doo, doo-doo-doo. ♪

11:16.630 --> 11:18.796
-(song ends)
-(whoops)

11:18.880 --> 11:20.380
(cheering, applause)

11:21.838 --> 11:23.755
♪ Chips, chips ♪

11:23.838 --> 11:26.005
Whoo!
♪ Doo, doo, doo-doo-doo ♪

11:26.088 --> 11:27.880
♪ Ci-boom, ci-boom, boom. ♪

11:27.963 --> 11:29.713
-WOMAN: Yes!
-(cheering)

11:30.796 --> 11:32.296
-Thanks so much.
-No problem.

11:32.380 --> 11:33.796
Good to see you, Vic.

11:33.880 --> 11:37.046
Hey, uh, two of those St-Germains
with the champagne drink things.

11:37.130 --> 11:38.671
BARTENDER:
Got you right there, boss.

11:38.755 --> 11:40.338
-Thank you.
-BARTENDER: No problem.

11:40.421 --> 11:41.963
How you doin', Vic?

11:42.046 --> 11:44.338
I'm fine. How are you?

11:44.421 --> 11:46.213
Eh, hangin' in there, bro.

11:53.005 --> 11:55.796
I just want to tell you two things, okay?

11:55.880 --> 11:57.296
Okay.

11:57.380 --> 12:00.296
I really want to repay you
for your abundant hospitality,

12:00.380 --> 12:01.880
you and your wife,

12:01.963 --> 12:05.255
as, you know, a stranger to the area.

12:05.338 --> 12:07.463
Sure.

12:07.546 --> 12:08.921
You've both been really cool.

12:09.005 --> 12:10.630
Really cool.

12:12.046 --> 12:13.713
The second?

12:13.796 --> 12:14.921
Huh?

12:15.005 --> 12:17.046
-The second thing you wanted to...
-Oh, man.

12:17.130 --> 12:18.546
I wanted to say, you're a brick

12:18.630 --> 12:21.338
for how nice you are
about me seeing your wife.

12:21.421 --> 12:24.463
(short laugh)
Seeing my wife.

12:26.338 --> 12:28.755
It's good to have a friend.

12:32.505 --> 12:34.505
I mean, it's all innocent, of course,
you know,

12:34.588 --> 12:38.005
but some guys, some husbands,

12:38.088 --> 12:40.338
-they get a little…
-Yeah, jealous.

12:40.421 --> 12:42.213
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

12:42.296 --> 12:46.046
Have you been around here long enough
where you've heard the name Martin McRae?

12:46.130 --> 12:49.380
Uh, the guy…
yeah, the guy who's gone missing.

12:49.463 --> 12:51.713
He saw a lot of my wife.

12:53.755 --> 12:55.463
What does that mean?

12:55.546 --> 12:58.213
He started seeing a lot of my wife.

13:01.338 --> 13:03.046
You suggesting…?

13:04.130 --> 13:05.880
They were friends.

13:08.880 --> 13:12.296
You want me to believe
you did something to Martin McRae?

13:14.005 --> 13:16.171
I killed him.

13:21.171 --> 13:22.838
Does Melinda know?

13:22.921 --> 13:24.338
Oh, God, no.

13:24.421 --> 13:26.088
She'd be horrified.

13:28.421 --> 13:30.505
All right, bro,

13:30.588 --> 13:31.963
considering he was a friend of yours,

13:32.046 --> 13:34.421
I don't think it's very funny
to joke about...

13:34.505 --> 13:36.713
He wasn't a friend of mine.

13:36.796 --> 13:38.213
A friend of your wife's.

13:38.296 --> 13:39.546
(chuckles):
Well...

13:39.630 --> 13:41.880
that's obviously something different,
isn't it?

13:44.963 --> 13:46.838
Are you, like, threatening me?

13:46.921 --> 13:49.296
Do you feel threatened?

13:52.421 --> 13:53.963
I don't believe you.

13:54.046 --> 13:56.338
Then don't.

14:01.213 --> 14:03.963
-("Dancing on My Own" by Robyn plays)
-(crowd chatter)

14:07.421 --> 14:08.546
I'll be right back.

14:08.630 --> 14:09.671
Joel?

14:13.630 --> 14:15.088
JOEL:
I'm going home.

14:15.171 --> 14:16.630
-What?
-I'll call you tomorrow.

14:16.713 --> 14:18.046
MELINDA:
What happened?

14:18.130 --> 14:20.630
♪ But I'm not the guy you're taking home ♪

14:20.713 --> 14:22.796
♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh ♪

14:22.880 --> 14:26.880
♪ I keep dancing on my own ♪

14:26.963 --> 14:29.755
♪ I keep dancing on... ♪

14:29.838 --> 14:31.755
(music continues muffled)

14:31.838 --> 14:33.838
-(people cheering)
-(balloons popping)

14:37.546 --> 14:40.046
MELINDA:
What did you say to Joel?

14:40.130 --> 14:41.546
Nothing.

14:43.421 --> 14:45.421
(laughs)

14:46.255 --> 14:48.046
You must've said something.

14:48.130 --> 14:49.546
No.

14:49.630 --> 14:51.005
I didn't say anything.

14:54.588 --> 14:57.713
Well, I saw you talking.

14:57.796 --> 14:59.255
What were you talking about?

14:59.338 --> 15:01.338
Bedbugs, maybe? No, that was Mary.

15:02.755 --> 15:04.296
(Melinda sighs)

15:04.380 --> 15:06.296
You're so weird.

15:08.338 --> 15:10.088
Would you like to get in the car?

15:16.880 --> 15:19.838
You must've said something...

15:19.921 --> 15:22.838
'cause he was different
after he talked to you.

15:23.921 --> 15:27.213
I promise you, I didn't.

15:29.421 --> 15:31.588
I don't believe you.

15:42.546 --> 15:44.546
♪ ♪

16:05.838 --> 16:07.505
(door closes)

16:07.588 --> 16:09.171
VIC:
So, uh...

16:09.255 --> 16:11.171
-five hours, right?
-CHELSEA: Yeah.

16:11.255 --> 16:13.005
-VIC: That's a hundred.
-Mm-hmm.

16:13.088 --> 16:15.463
-Venmo. I-I'll give you 200. How's that?
-Oh, sure.

16:15.546 --> 16:17.046
Melinda, what are you doing?

16:17.130 --> 16:19.755
-I'm gonna make coffee.
-I'll make you coffee.

16:19.838 --> 16:21.046
Go to bed. You're drunk.

16:21.130 --> 16:24.046
-I can do it.
-No, it's fine. I...

16:24.130 --> 16:27.088
Melinda… you're naked.

16:27.171 --> 16:28.171
What are you doing?

16:28.255 --> 16:30.713
-What?
-The babysitter's standing right there.

16:32.213 --> 16:33.755
-VIC: The babysitter.
-(Melinda scoffs)

16:33.838 --> 16:34.838
So what?

16:34.921 --> 16:37.338
-It's not appropriate.
-Jesus Christ.

16:37.421 --> 16:40.130
America is so suffocating.

16:40.213 --> 16:42.921
-(Melinda sighs)
-Sorry about that.

16:43.005 --> 16:45.921
-My wife's... a whole nother culture.
-Yeah, it's okay.

16:46.005 --> 16:47.796
(Melinda sighs)

16:51.046 --> 16:52.796
Thank you.

16:55.255 --> 16:58.963
I wish you'd pick someone
with some more brains.

17:01.005 --> 17:03.755
Is that what interests you in a woman?

17:04.838 --> 17:07.255
Her intelligence?

17:07.338 --> 17:10.505
That's one of the things, yes.

17:10.588 --> 17:12.588
Is that why you picked me?

17:12.671 --> 17:16.255
For my brains?

17:16.338 --> 17:18.421
You're very smart, Melinda.

17:18.505 --> 17:20.796
Yeah.

17:20.880 --> 17:23.796
Not in a way you respect.

17:29.046 --> 17:33.880
Joel might be dumb,
but me makes me enjoy who I am.

17:34.963 --> 17:37.505
(sighs)
And that turns me on.

17:41.255 --> 17:43.130
♪ ♪

17:46.921 --> 17:48.671
Vic.

17:53.963 --> 17:56.505
Close the door on your way out.

17:58.046 --> 17:59.963
(crickets chirping)

18:00.046 --> 18:02.046
♪ ♪

18:05.088 --> 18:07.213
(misters spraying)

18:15.838 --> 18:17.838
♪ ♪

18:23.838 --> 18:25.838
♪ ♪

18:38.880 --> 18:40.880
♪ ♪

18:50.130 --> 18:52.380
(whirring)

18:59.380 --> 19:00.671
(pills rattle)

19:00.755 --> 19:02.588
Thank you.

19:06.463 --> 19:08.671
Stick with it, Trix.

19:14.671 --> 19:16.505
(toy whirring)

19:20.755 --> 19:24.130
Did you know I had it on there wrong?

19:26.671 --> 19:29.130
Were you going to tell me?

19:29.213 --> 19:30.963
I didn't need to tell you, did I?

19:33.171 --> 19:35.171
In no time, you'll be like your dad,

19:35.255 --> 19:37.088
building bombs.

19:37.171 --> 19:39.046
-(quietly): Hmm.
-(toy whirs)

19:39.130 --> 19:40.338
TRIXIE:
Dad doesn't build bombs.

19:40.421 --> 19:43.130
He made a computer chip.

19:49.963 --> 19:51.213
("You Make Me Feel Like Dancing"
by Leo Sayer playing)

19:51.296 --> 19:54.380
♪ You've got a cute way of talking ♪

19:55.546 --> 19:59.338
♪ You've got the better of me ♪

20:00.546 --> 20:02.505
♪ Just hold me tight ♪

20:02.588 --> 20:04.963
♪ And leave on the light ♪

20:06.005 --> 20:09.505
♪ 'Cause I don't wanna go home ♪

20:10.713 --> 20:13.088
♪ You've put a spell on me ♪

20:13.171 --> 20:15.630
♪ I'm right where you want me to be ♪

20:15.713 --> 20:19.046
VIC and TRIXIE:
♪ You make me feel like dancing... ♪

20:19.130 --> 20:21.546
-VIC: So, you have music today, right?
-(kids chattering)

20:21.630 --> 20:22.880
TRIXIE:
Yes.

20:22.963 --> 20:24.880
-VIC: Does that mean violin?
-Yes.

20:24.963 --> 20:26.380
-Will that be fun?
-Yes.

20:26.463 --> 20:27.546
VIC (chuckles):
Okay.

20:27.630 --> 20:29.838
Have a good day. I love you!

20:29.921 --> 20:31.921
Love you!

20:33.546 --> 20:36.005
MAN: Your mom is gonna get you
after school, all right?

20:36.088 --> 20:37.671
CHILD:
I'm coming!

20:37.755 --> 20:39.755
(chattering continues)

20:41.005 --> 20:42.380
KRISTIN:
Vic!

20:42.463 --> 20:44.421
Vic!

20:46.213 --> 20:47.796
What?

20:47.880 --> 20:49.921
You're running around murdering people

20:50.005 --> 20:52.505
and you don't call me
to help cover up the crime scene?

20:52.588 --> 20:54.046
-It was a joke.
-Yeah.

20:54.130 --> 20:55.713
I should fucking hope so.

20:56.796 --> 20:57.880
How'd you hear about it?

20:57.963 --> 20:59.880
(sighs) I've heard about it
from so many people now,

20:59.963 --> 21:01.880
I honest to God don't remember
who told me first.

21:01.963 --> 21:03.505
Jesus Christ.

21:04.796 --> 21:07.088
But, boy, did it work.

21:07.171 --> 21:08.630
(Kristin chuckling)

21:13.838 --> 21:15.338
